  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Dilution",
      "excerpt": "Dilution If you invest in our Ordinary\nShares, your interest will be diluted to the extent of the difference between the initial public offering price per Ordinary Share\nand our net tangible book value per Ordinary Share after this offering. Dilution results from the fact that the initial public\noffering price per Ordinary Share is substantially in excess of the book value per Ordinary Share attributable to the existing\nshareholders for our presently outstanding Ordinary Share. Our net tangible book value\nas of March 31, 2026 was US$720,575, or US$0.09 per Ordinary Share, as adjusted. Net tangible book value represents the\namount of our total consolidated tangible assets, less the amount of our total consolidated liabilities. Dilution is determined by subtracting\nnet tangible book value per Ordinary Share, after giving effect to the additional proceeds we will receive from this offering,",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    }
  ],
